WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.600
Speaker 1: So there are many people who have
been hoping for waiting for praying for even

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:12.719
the demise of Joe Biden, and they are really
going to have to keep waiting, quite frankly,

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:19.860
at least for now, as Joe Biden's approval
rating has jumped to 63 percent, up two points

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.430
from late March.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:29.590
This is not about cheerleading or praising
when there is nothing to praise, but it is

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:35.940
about understanding why Joe Biden's approval
rating is up again, but also importantly,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:42.179
the areas where it's not because they actually
are cause for concern and show that the Republican

00:00:42.179 --> 00:00:46.090
strategy has actually worked where they have
applied it.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.370
And we're going to get to all of that.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:55.239
But the data is that a new poll from the Associated
Press and NORC now has Joe Biden at 63 percent

00:00:55.239 --> 00:01:00.199
approval, overall, 96 percent approval among
Democrats.

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:03.649
Trump would often tout 96 percent approval
from Republicans.

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:05.440
We could never find that data.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.700
Joe Biden really has 96 percent approval from
Democrats.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:18.180
AP NORC poll, 62 percent approval from independents
and yes, a paltry 23 percent approval among

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.180
Republicans.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:25.360
But that is dramatically higher than Democratic
approval of Trump threw out Donald Trump's

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.360
presidency.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:32.040
These are notable Republican approval numbers
for how how high they are, even at 23 percent.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.910
And overall, this puts Joe Biden at 63 percent
approval.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:41.930
Now, in this poll, the number of Americans
who are optimistic about the country's direction

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.750
is up to 54 percent.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:49.780
We had a different poll yesterday which had
that number at 40 percent, up from 20 percent.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.060
This poll asked the question a little differently.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.890
And has Joe has the country at 54 percent
thinking we are moving in the right direction.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:04.480
This is the highest of any AP poll dating
back to the beginning of Donald Trump's presidency.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:10.969
In other words, the country is more optimistic
today than at any time during the Trump presidency.

00:02:10.969 --> 00:02:13.829
What is pushing Joe Biden's approval rating
up?

00:02:13.829 --> 00:02:18.189
The issues are handling of the covid pandemic.

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:24.049
Health care and the economy, according to
this very same poll, some of this is logical,

00:02:24.049 --> 00:02:25.459
some of it is more notable.

00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:31.879
For example, Democrats tend not to poll as
well on the economy, despite the fact that

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:36.739
the economy by every indicator does better
when a Democrat is in the White House rather

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:38.049
than a Republican.

00:02:38.049 --> 00:02:44.900
That's interesting, 71 percent of Americans
approve of Joe Biden's handling of the pandemic.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.930
And we are getting closer and closer to ending
the pandemic.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.319
I'm going to have the latest numbers for you.

00:02:50.319 --> 00:02:52.859
Probably tomorrow, maybe Thursday.

00:02:52.859 --> 00:02:57.680
The last week has seen even faster declines
in cases, even faster declines in deaths.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.909
Fortunately, an uptick in vaccination.

00:02:59.909 --> 00:03:02.969
And we will get to that a little bit later
in the week.

00:03:02.969 --> 00:03:08.519
Even 47 percent of Republicans approve of
Joe Biden's handling of the pandemic.

00:03:08.519 --> 00:03:13.760
57 percent of Americans approve of Joe Biden's
handling of the economy.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:19.650
62 percent approve of Joe Biden's handling
of health care so far, which has been mostly

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:24.670
prioritizing the Affordable Care Act and a
few things tied in with covid stimulus.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.959
Not that much has actually been done yet as
far as health care goes.

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:30.390
So consider that disconnect right now.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:36.549
Joe Biden's approval rating is high because
of his handling of covid and the economic

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.749
stimulus.

00:03:37.749 --> 00:03:46.379
And yet zero Republicans, not few zero Republicans
voted for that very same covid stimulus.

00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:51.810
That is part of why Joe Biden is popular,
even with a relatively high number of Republicans.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:58.011
Now, on the flip side, Joe Biden is not at
50 percent approval on two major issues, gun

00:03:58.011 --> 00:04:01.019
policy and immigration.

00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:08.510
This is super important because these aren't
two issues on which Joe Biden has just naturally

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.650
struggled to build approval.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:18.639
Those two issues, gun safety and immigration,
are the issues that Republicans have chosen

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:20.600
to attack Joe Biden over.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:26.610
This means that the Republican counter narratives,
the right wing media, counter narratives do

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.610
work.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:32.729
They do influence people's thinking and people's
opinions and beliefs almost from day one.

00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:38.500
I mean that literally day one, I think it
was day five of the Biden presidency, Republicans

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:43.110
and Peter Doocy from Fox News and others started
the counternarrative on immigration.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.699
The border is chaos.

00:04:44.699 --> 00:04:46.020
There's kids in cages.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.599
There's kids separated from their parents.

00:04:47.599 --> 00:04:50.389
All of the things they didn't care about when
Trump was president.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:51.849
And it has worked.

00:04:51.849 --> 00:04:56.120
It has worked to build the belief that there's
a crisis on immigration and that at least

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.930
to some degree, it's Joe Biden's fault.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:04.080
There were I think it was back in June, 28
percent of Americans believe there was an

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.100
immigration crisis.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.890
Now it's 48 percent.

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:11.080
Not much has actually changed other than Republicans
have been hammering this issue.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:16.770
Second issue on which Joe Biden is not doing
well is gun control.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:19.250
Biden has done almost nothing on gun control.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:24.410
Understand that after that recent string of
mass shootings, Joe Biden did announce he

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.919
was going to be going after the government
will go after ghost guns a little more and

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:33.569
some very tame, like very, very minor gun
safety issues, some of which may not even

00:05:33.569 --> 00:05:38.949
lead to anything because they were Biden saying,
please study this and tell me what to do.

00:05:38.949 --> 00:05:44.050
So we need to understand that when you and
I start to see these narratives pop up on

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:49.290
Fox News and Newsmax and Lindsey Graham is
talking about it and whatever we know, they're

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.640
fabricated out of thin air.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:56.009
And we know there's often nothing to them,
but they work and they can be a drag on presidential

00:05:56.009 --> 00:05:57.009
approval.

00:05:57.009 --> 00:06:02.810
Now, in terms of Joe Biden's 63 percent approval
overall, yeah, to some degree, the American

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.560
people are realizing that some things are
going well.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:12.700
Republicans have been complaining that Joe
Biden's tweeting is too boring and too conventional.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.729
That's a sign they don't have much to complain
about.

00:06:14.729 --> 00:06:21.810
We covered that segment on Fox News last week,
which I called Is the economy doing too well

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:22.870
under Biden?

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:26.190
And that's when, you know, things are going
OK economically.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:31.090
And it's pushing Joe Biden's approval up beyond
where Trump ever was during his presidency.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:35.710
Remember Trump never achieving 50 percent
approval even once during his presidency.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:39.590
Joe Biden was at one now at 63.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:40.819
That's good.

00:06:40.819 --> 00:06:46.210
But we have to understand that whatever they
can get purchase on, traction on.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.759
And right now that's guns and immigration.

00:06:48.759 --> 00:06:52.439
They will use it to try to win in 2022.

00:06:52.439 --> 00:07:26.110
And we simply have to be ready 

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:48.710
for it.

